l":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Internal_hallucinations"},{"name":"Memory suppression","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Memory_suppression"},{"name":"Motor control loss","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Motor_control_loss"},{"name":"Novelty enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Novelty_enhancement"},{"name":"Pattern recognition enhancement","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Pattern_recognition_enhancement"},{"name":"Perception of increased weight","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Perception_of_increased_weight"},{"name":"Perspective alterations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Perspective_alterations"},{"name":"Physical euphoria","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Physical_euphoria"},{"name":"Pupil dilation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Pupil_dilation"},{"name":"Scenarios and plots","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Scenarios_and_plots"},{"name":"Sedation","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Sedation"},{"name":"Settings, sceneries, and landscapes","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Settings,_sceneries,_and_landscapes"},{"name":"Spontaneous tactile sensations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Spontaneous_tactile_sensations"},{"name":"Subconscious communication","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Subconscious_communication"},{"name":"Thought acceleration","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_acceleration"},{"name":"Thought connectivity","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Thought_connectivity"},{"name":"Time distortion","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Time_distortion"},{"name":"Transformations","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Transformations"},{"name":"Unity and interconnectedness","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Unity_and_interconnectedness"},{"name":"Vasoconstriction","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Vasoconstriction"},{"name":"Wakefulness","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Wakefulness"},{"name":"Euphoria"},{"name":"Empathy"},{"name":"Insight"},{"name":"Brightened colour"},{"name":"Closed/Open eye visuals"},{"name":"Enhanced tactile sensation"},{"name":"Mental/physical stimulation"},{"name":"Decreased appetite"},{"name":"Restlessness"},{"name":"Change in perception"},{"name":"Ego softening"},{"name":"Sweating/chills"},{"name":"Muscle tension"},{"name":"Confusion"},{"name":"Insomnia"}],"combinations":[{"substance":"Lithium","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Tramadol","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Cannabis","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Stimulants","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/LSA"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/lsa"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_LSA.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ergine"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on LSA","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2041643"}],"wikidata":"Q2041643","pharmacology":{"text":"Ergine interacts with serotonin, dopamine, and adrenergic receptors similarly to but with lower affinity than lysergic acid diethylamide (LSD). It is known to act as an agonist of the serotonin 5-HT2A and 5-HT2B receptors similarly to LSD, albeit much less potently and with reduced activational efficacy. The drug has about 4.3% of the antiserotonergic activity of LSD in the isolated rat uterus in vitro.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Ergine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ergine#Pharmacodynamics","kind":"Serotonin receptor agonist; Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen; Sedative","body":[{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Hepatic"},{"what":"leaves","says":"Urine"}],"figures":"Ergine"},"uses":{"text":"Ergine is most commonly used as a drug in the form of morning glory seeds, including those of Ipomoea tricolor (tlitliltzin), Ipomoea corymbosa (ololiuhqui), and Argyreia nervosa (Hawaiian baby woodrose). They may be consumed whole and intact, crushed or ground up, or drunk as an extract following soaking of the seeds in water.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Ergine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ergine#Use","routes":"Oral, intramuscular injection, subcutaneous injection","figures":"Ergine"},"sideEffects":{"text":"A 2016 study showed that penniclavine was the predominant alkaloid in Ipomoea tricolor seeds. Ergoclavines are known to cause convulsive ergotism, the milder form of ergotism. Gangrenous ergotism is caused by ergopeptines: the complex peptide moiety forces persistence at the receptor sites.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Ergine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ergine#Side_effects"},"formula":"C16H17N3O","molarMass":267.33}